      "body": "## Motivation\n\nDynamic EPLB migrates expert weights between ranks with NCCL point-to-point operations.\n\nThe Humming/MXFP4 MoE backend stores some expert scale tensors as `torch.float8_e8m0fnu`. PyTorch's NCCL process group cannot send or receive this dtype directly, so the first dynamic EPLB rebalance fails with:\n\n```text\nTypeError: Input tensor data type is not supported for NCCL process group:\nFloat8_e8m0fnu\n```\n\nThe tensor payload is byte-addressable and does not require numerical conversion during migration.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Add `_get_p2p_transport_tensor()` to return a zero-copy `torch.uint8` view for `torch.float8_e8m0fnu` tensors.\n- Apply the transport view symmetrically to EPLB P2P send and receive buffers.\n- Leave NCCL-supported tensor dtypes and tensor objects unchanged.\n- Add a registered CPU unit test covering:\n  - E8M0 tensors use a `uint8` transport view;\n  - the transport view shares the original storage;\n  - the E8M0 byte pattern is preserved;\n  - writes through a receive-side view update the original tensor;\n  - supported dtypes are returned unchanged.\n\nThis changes only the transport representation. It does not cast, requantize, or alter the expert tensor contents.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nEnd-to-end smoke test:\n\n- Model: DeepSeek-V4-Pro\n- GPU: H20\n- MoE runner backend: Humming\n- MoE A2A backend: DeepEP\n- Dynamic EPLB: enabled\n- GSM8K samples: 20\n\n```text\nAccuracy: 0.950\nInvalid: 0.000\nLatency: 15.308 s\nOutput throughput: 136.723 token/s\n```\n\nThe test completed after dynamic EPLB migration without the previous NCCL dtype failure.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo steady-state inference path is changed. The helper creates a zero-copy dtype view only while constructing dynamic EPLB migration P2P operations:\n\n```python\ntensor.view(torch.uint8)\n```\n\nIt performs no allocation or data conversion. Therefore no steady-state throughput regression is expected. The end-to-end smoke test above confirms successful inference with dynamic EPLB enabled.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (No user-facing behavior or configuration is changed.)\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #34452419639](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/34452419639)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #34452419333](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/34452419333)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd-rocm720:start -->:x: [Run #34452419503](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/34452419503)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd-rocm720:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
